 "discovery_answer": "I registered the services the agent calls. The test hasn't started yet. `nookku register` printed:\n\n```\nnookku: the egress answer is registered. The next start uses these parts:\n- model API anthropic: ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL -> the URL in ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL or the default (proxy)\n- MCP server catalog: http CATALOG_MCP_URL -> http://127.0.0.1:9310/mcp (proxy)\n- MCP server notes: stdio NOTES_MCP_COMMAND -> python3 notes_mcp.py (proxy)\n- database shop: postgres, DATABASE_URL (proxy)\n- database returns: sqlite, returns.db (driver trace)\n```\n\nNotes on these parts:\n- **Model API:** The Claude Agent SDK session in `app.py` doesn't set a URL, so this is `null` and uses `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` or the default.\n- **No HTTP backends and no other parts:** The agent doesn't call any.\n- **Not listed:**\n  - The `shop` MCP server runs inside the agent's own process (`create_sdk_mcp_server`), so it isn't an outside service.\n  - `notes.json` is a file the notes MCP server writes itself, so the MCP proxy records those calls.\n- **Driver trace for `returns.db`:** I didn't change any code. `app.py:45-69` already sets up OpenTelemetry for both psycopg and sqlite3 and sends spans over HTTP to the OTLP endpoint when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set. The sqlite3 instrumentation includes the statement text by default. A driver trace has no result rows and may hide parameter values. Here that means the `INSERT INTO returns` record may show `?` where the order, SKU and reason would be.\n\nPlease check these parts. If they're right, type `nookku start` within the next 30 minutes. If one is wrong, tell me what to fix and I'll register it again.",
